{"first_web": "firecrawl", "used_firecrawl": true, "used_native": false, "skills": ["firecrawl", "firecrawl-scrape"], "fc_cmds": ["scrape"], "fc_api": [], "n_tools": 3, "tools": ["shell", "shell", "shell"], "num_turns": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 63116, "cached_input_tokens": 40320, "output_tokens": 408}, "cost_usd": 0.0376, "result_subtype": "success", "error": null, "answer": "The article describes five workflow patterns:\n\n1. **Prompt chaining** \u2014 Break a task into sequential steps, with each LLM call using the previous call\u2019s output. Optional checks validate intermediate results.\n2. **Routing** \u2014 Classify an input and send it to a specialized process, prompt, or model.\n3. **Parallelization** \u2014 Run calls simultaneously and combine their outputs, using either independent subtasks (**sectioning**) or repeated attempts (**voting**).\n4. **Orchestrator-workers** \u2014 A central LLM dynamically divides a task, delegates work to other LLMs, and synthesizes their results.\n5. **Evaluator-optimizer** \u2014 One LLM generates an answer while another evaluates it, providing feedback for iterative improvement.\n\nThe article separately discusses **augmented LLMs** as the foundational building block and **autonomous agents** as systems that dynamically control their own processes and tool use.\n\nSource: [Anthropic \u2014 Building effective agents](https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/building-effective-agents).", "correct": true, "id": "t05", "trial": 1, "duration_s": 13.8, "timed_out": false, "stderr": "Reading additional input from stdin...\n", "outputs": ["README.md", "notes.txt"]}
