{"first_web": "firecrawl", "used_firecrawl": true, "used_native": false, "skills": ["firecrawl-scrape"], "fc_cmds": ["scrape"], "fc_api": [], "n_tools": 3, "tools": ["shell", "shell", "shell"], "num_turns": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 74482, "cached_input_tokens": 57984, "output_tokens": 414}, "cost_usd": 0.032, "result_subtype": "success", "error": null, "answer": "The article describes five workflow patterns:\n\n1. **Prompt chaining:** Break a task into sequential steps, with each LLM call using the previous call\u2019s output. Optional checks validate intermediate results.\n2. **Routing:** Classify an input and send it to a specialized prompt, model, or process.\n3. **Parallelization:** Run LLM calls simultaneously and combine their results. Two variants are **sectioning** (independent subtasks) and **voting** (multiple attempts at the same task).\n4. **Orchestrator-workers:** A central LLM dynamically determines subtasks, delegates them to worker LLMs, and synthesizes their results.\n5. **Evaluator-optimizer:** One LLM generates an answer while another evaluates it, providing feedback for iterative refinement.\n\nThe article separately discusses the **augmented LLM** as a foundational building block and **autonomous agents** as systems that dynamically control their own process.\n\nSource: [Anthropic \u2014 Building effective agents](https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/building-effective-agents)", "correct": true, "id": "t05", "trial": 3, "duration_s": 16.2, "timed_out": false, "stderr": "Reading additional input from stdin...\n", "outputs": ["README.md", "notes.txt"]}
